When I first played this game I was very disapointed about it so in the first place I gave it a negative review. The negative review came because of the hard grind for weapons and especially for silver. When you start playing this game you should already know or be advised on how to spend your credits wisely just because you will be tempted to buy a lot of attachments, guns or even vehicles. You need to be reserved in spending silver credits and do the things right. I will now point some features for this game that are good and bad and put them in balance.
Good Features:
-Diversity in everything related to weapons, attachments, vechicles, cammouflages and more;
-World War II Theme suited for the ones that are looking for a good MMO-FPS game based on this subject;
-Some historical accuracy;
-Game-Modes are decent, only 4 but good enough for this kind of game. You can play from close-quarters battles to real-large battles that involves: vehicles, tanks, planes, recon teams, paratroopers etc.;
-You have the opportunity to play different roles like tanker, recon, paratrooper, pilot, infantry in a First Person perspective (so I want to call this game an FPS). You can control tanks and take part in intense battles of 2 WWII major armies;
-Maps are made well on overall but there are some little problems of balance;
-Gameplay is fun but here depends on how you see the things and I think for this game is a chance of 50% to like the gameplay...for me I found it fun;
-Sound is decent but could be better;
-Graphics is not amazing/stunning at all but it is a clean and decent one...so graphics for this game are decent;
-Optimization is great and especially on storage as long as this game occupy under 1.3 GB on disk;
-Is a simple game, easy to learn and to play;
-Developers work for their game, you get often updates and events. Often you receive free Veteran membership and gold that can boost your XP/Credits gained;
-Player ranking system where you get placed in matchmaking according to what rank you are. This feature also help you unlock some extra credits, 500 gold and some veteran days(premium account to boost);
-Team spirit if you have luck of good teammates;
Bad Features:
-Grind could be hard and could make you quit the game easily. Although you have to play it for a while untill you unlock some items and untill game becomes very enjoyable and fun...this could make you see the game as a pay2win. Also when you have veteran membership you level up decent and this problem is resolved;
-Some mechanics are poor and I will give one example: when you crouch/prone you can't stand up back by pressing jump button like in other FPS games and you need to press the same button you crouched/proned twice to get up back;
-Game could be very frustating when you buy something and you discover you don't like it or is not good/suited for you. That is because when you buy someting you don't get enough  information on how is going to be or what minuses has in comparisson with what you already have. This is very true when you switch career from infantry to a recon for example and you find out after bought and spend well worked credits on this career that you have minus 4 slot points for your weapons to carry and maybe you don't like this. They should add a test or preview feature for everything you buy in this game or you should have the right to get the things back along with the money spend within 1 hour of playing with the specific bought weapon/career;
-Balance is a problem at least in some battles;
-I have the feeling that game forces you to buy and play how it wants sometimes. For example when you get the first tank at US for free you can't do armor damage ribbon just because the first tank has only machine-guns so you can't make damage with a cannon and you are forced to buy expensive tanks to unlock that ribbon and that's because stuart is slow too due to low damage from the main cannon;
-Some items are really expensive. I think a handgun should cost lower than almost 80000 credits;
-It is a game where you have to spend real-money or your time. Your choice;
-We need more maps especially on Skirmish and why not on Encounter. Could be good if we can have some specific climate maps based on snow or rain;
I will stop here and I will take in account that game is currently in BETA and things may be slightly better in the future. It is a free2play game and is not bad at all. You can try it and the most important thing is that you are not forced to spend real-money in-game so you can play it for free entirely but you need to spend some time then. I chose to recommend this title as long as I had fun by playing it and you can try it to for making an opinion about it. If you are looking for a nice FPS based on World War II you should give this a try. (70/100 for me)

I really wanted to like this game, I really did, but there were so many things going on that took away any feelings of joy or satisfaction from this game.  I ended up asking for refund as a result after a few hours of giving it chances to improve but all that ended up happening was a lowering of my expectations and that's not fun.
Navigating the ship around was a choir and rather unintuitive;
Combat felt the same way due to poor camera controls and the fact that enemy ships would continuously whiz past me and the only way I could keep them in a firing arc was to slow my ship down to the point that I was now a sitting duck;
The missions and campaign were supremely boring and I didn’t even bother reading any of the text outlines for them at one point;
Control placement on the middle mouse button are inconvenient as well since the scroll wheel is how you increase/decrease ship speed which ended up getting in the way more often than not;
The UI overall was in the way really.  No readouts on speed beyond a thin bar at the bottom of the screen, poor indications on directional headings, the ship hangar/loadout screens are just an unorganized mess.
Everything about this game feels like this wants to be EVE without actually going to the trouble of putting forth any effort to make that happen.  Definitely a softball pitch that bounces five feet in front of the plate.

